1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,079
A planetary system is one star and all the objects held in orbit around it by gravity: planets, moons,

2
00:00:06,079 --> 00:00:12,098
comets, asteroids and tiny bits of ice and rock. Ours is the Solar System, with the Sun at its centre.

3
00:00:13,157 --> 00:00:16,049
Eight planets orbit the Sun in elliptical paths.

4
00:00:16,049 --> 00:00:22,128
Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars are rocky planets; Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune are gas planets.

5
00:00:22,128 --> 00:00:24,488
All except Mercury and Venus have moons.

6
00:00:25,547 --> 00:00:30,210
Planets and moons are non-luminous: we see them because they reflect sunlight.

7
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:33,987
That's why stars twinkle but planets shine with a steady light.

8
00:00:33,987 --> 00:00:39,062
Astronomers have found over four thousand other stars with planets, called exoplanets.

9
00:00:40,121 --> 00:00:45,550
NASA's planetary fact sheet gives the time each planet takes to travel once around the Sun,

10
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,967
measured in Earth years.

11
00:00:48,026 --> 00:00:53,219
Mercury takes less than a quarter of a year, Earth takes one year, and Mars almost two.

12
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:56,406
But Jupiter takes about 12 years and Saturn nearly 30.

13
00:00:57,465 --> 00:01:04,724
Pause and decide: what is the pattern between a planet's distance from the Sun and the time it takes to complete one orbit?

14
00:01:05,783 --> 00:01:12,098
About 4.6 billion years ago, the Solar System formed from a nebula: a giant cloud of gas and stellar dust.

15
00:01:12,098 --> 00:01:18,471
Gravity pulled it inwards and it began to spin, forming a hot protostar at the centre, which became the Sun.

16
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:24,488
Around it, dust and rock stuck together into protoplanets, which grew into planets.

17
00:01:24,488 --> 00:01:29,976
Rocks left over became asteroids. Most orbit between Mars and Jupiter, in the asteroid belt,

18
00:01:29,976 --> 00:01:33,576
where Jupiter's strong gravity stopped them forming a planet.

19
00:01:34,635 --> 00:01:40,714
Dwarf planets are bigger than asteroids but smaller than planets, and gravity has rounded their shape.

20
00:01:40,714 --> 00:01:47,029
Pluto was reclassified as a dwarf planet in 2006. Beyond Neptune lies the Kuiper Belt, full of icy objects.

21
00:01:48,088 --> 00:01:52,396
Comets are made of ice, dust and rock and follow very long, thin orbits.

22
00:01:52,396 --> 00:01:58,061
Near the Sun, the ice turns to gas, releasing dust that the Sun's radiation pushes into a tail.

23
00:01:58,061 --> 00:02:01,012
So a comet's tail always points away from the Sun.
